nodes.body:
@AndreasKaratzas @qli88 re:
>for aiter_on only, either use the fp32-accumulating RMSNorm path @divakar-amd pointed to (use_model_sensitive_rmsnorm), or apply a wider tolerance with a comment explaining why.

We don't use `use_model_sensitive_rmsnorm=1` anywhere in vLLM afaik, so it would be better to find a way to test the same way we run in production IMO (with `use_model_sensitive_rmsnorm=0`). Unless there is a really good reason to test this (e.g. matching the precision of the reference impl), let's try to avoid that.

